{"id":"int-2b921c44c74d789a9c27b4d5aafc3ba9","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-08-28T11:48:16.398432Z","actor":"Eric Bowman","issue_id":"gateopener-f8w.1","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Root cause found with screenshot and log evidence: OverlayWindowController.handleOpening() never calls setContent(_:), so on a reopen the panel keeps the PREVIOUS session's DoorVideoFrameView (already holding a decoded image) and show() re-fires overlayWillShow() on it. Both symptoms trace to that one omission. Refuted the earlier 'animation torn out mid-play' theory: the 2.2s canned clip finishes long before .streaming arrives at ~6s, so on a FIRST open it plays fully; on a reopen it is never re-installed at all. View Door path is unaffected because DoorVideoOverlayController.start() calls setContent(connecting) synchronously every time. Recorded as bd memory gateopener-f8w-root-cause-gate-open-path-overlaywindowcontro. Diagnosis only, no production diff."}}
